M9.1 Relay-Blindness Evidence
============================

Topology:
Alice -> Bob -> Carol

Bob is the forwarding relay.

Observed APP_DATA evidence includes routing/protocol metadata such as:
- packet type = APP_DATA
- source identity
- destination identity
- packet ID
- TTL
- session ID
- sequence number
- ciphertext length

The relay observation contains ciphertext rather than endpoint plaintext.
Carol successfully receives and decrypts the message at the endpoint.

Session-ownership statement:
Bob's implemented session manager does not contain the Alice–Carol endpoint
application session required to decrypt the packet.

This is the precise implementation-level claim supported by the evidence. It is
not a claim that a compromised relay can never possess endpoint keys by some
other means.

Architecture boundary:
- routing forwards opaque APP_DATA
- endpoint application/session logic performs decryption
- no production routing-layer DecryptMessage path is used for APP_DATA
- M9.1 test observation is local test wrapping of the existing message callback,
